sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Thompson published no equations, so fidelity is to his words and figure. \"Coaxial circles\" is formalised as the Moebius group, the only maps that carry straight lines to circles, and the script states that reading in the docstring; because Fig. 376's two pencils meet obliquely, a second family (affine then Moebius) is fitted so that the figure as drawn is covered and not only its stated idealisation. The alternative Thompson compares against (\"rectilinear co-ordinates\", i.e. the identity/similarity) and the one he does not (affine) are fitted the same way, and the exact deformation is the thin-plate spline of Bookstein 1989, the standard successor to the method. The fitters are checked on synthetic maps before the real fit. Not higher because Thompson's own drawn grid is not digitised and compared with the fitted one (the comparison is grid-family to data, not his constants to the fitted constants); because his \"typical Scaroid fish\" and unnamed Pomacanthus are replaced by genus Procrustes means, which is the right test of the general claim but not of his drawing; and because the fish are 17 landmarks, not the outline Thompson deformed, so curvature between landmarks is untested. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L5–L23: the claim quoted; the reading of coaxial circles as a Moebius map <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L5-L23>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L47–L66: what is computed: the five families, noise floor, context, LOO <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L47-L66>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L210–L269: moebius()/fit_moebius()/coaxial()/fit_coaxial(): the two coaxial families, started from the affine fit, several c starts <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L210-L269>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L272–L290: tps_fit()/tps_apply(): Bookstein 1989 with bending energy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L272-L290>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L305–L313: self_test(): known maps recovered <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3cf7f8c/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L305-L313>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species (thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Model fidelity to source' for Scarus (22 spp.) and Pomacanthus (9 spp.), with Chaetodon (54 spp.) and 59 other genera for context; Indo-Pacific shore fishes, lateral view" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor agent)" .
}

